+# Budget Recovery Runbook
+
+Emergency procedure for recovering Amazon Ads portfolio budgets from guidance data.
+
+**Script:** `scripts/ops/budget_recovery.py`
+**Story:** STORY-639
+
+---
+
+## When to use this runbook
+
+Use this procedure when portfolio budgets have drifted from guidance (e.g., after an
+outage, cron failure, or incorrect bulk update) and need to be restored manually.
+
+---
+
+## 5-Step Recovery Procedure
+
+### Step 1 — Verify credentials
+
+Ensure you are logged in to the Azure CLI and have access to the Key Vault:
+
+```bash
+az login
+az keyvault secret list --vault-name kv-mcp-ads --query "[].name" -o tsv
+```
+
+If secrets are not accessible, contact the platform team before proceeding.
+
+### Step 2 — Generate the recovery plan (dry run)
+
+Run `--dry-run` to compute the plan without writing anything to Amazon:
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/ops/budget_recovery.py --dry-run
+```
+
+Review the plan output. Confirm the list of portfolios and deltas is correct.
+
+Optionally filter to a single parent:
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/ops/budget_recovery.py --dry-run --parent GG-StretchFilm-Parent
+```
+
+### Step 3 — Export plan to CSV for approval
+
+Use `--csv-only` to write the plan to a CSV file without making any Amazon API calls:
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/ops/budget_recovery.py --csv-only
+# Plan written to /tmp/budget_recovery_plan.csv
+```
+
+Share `/tmp/budget_recovery_plan.csv` with ops lead for sign-off before proceeding.
+
+### Step 4 — Apply the pre-approved plan
+
+Once the plan CSV has been reviewed and approved, apply it with `--from-csv --apply`:
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/ops/budget_recovery.py --from-csv /tmp/budget_recovery_plan.csv --apply
+```
+
+Alternatively, apply directly with guards to prevent accidental large cuts:
+
+```bash
+python3 scripts/ops/budget_recovery.py --apply \
+    --threshold-pct 5 \
+    --max-decrease-pct 30 \
+    --limit 10
+```
+
+Use `--apply` only after reviewing the dry-run output and obtaining approval.
+
+### Step 5 — Verify and record
+
+After applying:
+
+1. Check the output summary: `succeeded=N  failed=0`
+2. Review `/tmp/budget_recovery_results.csv` for per-portfolio status
+3. Confirm budgets in Amazon Ads console or via API spot-check
+4. Log the incident with plan hash and operator name in the on-call notes
+
+---
+
+## Safety guards
+
+| Flag | Purpose |
+|------|---------|
+| `--dry-run` | Show plan, no Amazon writes |
+| `--csv-only` | Write plan CSV, zero Amazon calls |
+| `--from-csv FILE` | Replay pre-approved plan only |
+| `--limit N` | Cap at N portfolios for staged rollout |
+| `--threshold-pct N` | Skip changes smaller than N% of current cap |
+| `--max-decrease-pct N` | Block decreases larger than N% of current cap |
+
+---
+
+## Audit trail
+
+Every `--apply` run should be logged in `manual_recovery_log` via `write_recovery_log()`.
+Check the database after a run:
+
+```sql
+SELECT operator, plan_path, succeeded, failed, executed_at
+FROM manual_recovery_log
+ORDER BY executed_at DESC
+LIMIT 5;
+```
+
+---
+
